-- title:
--   Tangent coordinates across a commuting square of lifts
-- statement:
--   Let $T'$ be an Artinian local ring with residue field $k =$ `ResidueField T'`, let $I \subseteq \mathfrak{m}_{T'}$ be an ideal with $I\cdot\mathfrak{m}_{T'} = 0$, and let $V$ be a finite-dimensional $k$-module, equipped also with a right $k$-action acting centrally and with a $T'$-module structure compatible via the residue map, together with an injective $T'$-linear map $\iota : V \to T'$ whose range is $I$ viewed as a $T'$-submodule. Let $C$ be a flat $T'$-algebra, $q_Y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} T'$ a scheme over $T'$, and $u : \operatorname{Spec} C \to Y$ a morphism over $T'$. Let $x_k : A_k \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ carry a relative group law $L_k$ (functorial multiplication, unit, inverse on points over $k$-schemes, with associativity, unit and inverse laws and naturality), let $a_k : A_k \to Y$ exhibit $A_k$ as the fibre product of $Y$ with $\operatorname{Spec} k$ over $\operatorname{Spec} T'$, let $U_e \subseteq A_k$ be an affine open, and let $e_1 : \operatorname{Spec} k \to U_e$ be a point of $U_e$ whose composite with the inclusion is the unit section of $L_k$ over the identity. Let $\psi_0, \psi_1 : C \to C$ be $T'$-algebra endomorphisms each congruent to the identity modulo the ideal generated by the image of $I$ in $C$, and let $v_T, v_{T'}, v_{A_0}, v_{A_1} : \operatorname{Spec} C \to Y$ satisfy: $v_{T'}$ and $v_{A_1}$ are morphisms over $T'$, $v_{A_0} = u \circ \operatorname{Spec}\psi_0$, $v_T = u \circ \operatorname{Spec}\psi_1$, and $v_{T'} \circ \operatorname{Spec}\psi_0 = v_{A_1} \circ \operatorname{Spec}\psi_1$. Finally let $c_s, c_s', b_0, b_1$ be maps from $\Gamma(A_k, U_e)$ to the $k$-linear maps $\operatorname{Hom}_k(V^\vee, k \otimes_{T'} C)$, each satisfying `IsTangentCoordsOfPairAt` for the pairs $(u, v_T)$, $(u, v_{T'})$, $(u, v_{A_0})$, $(u, v_{A_1})$ respectively: that is, for each there are a morphism $w_0$ from the spectrum of the thickening $(k \otimes_{T'} C) \otimes_k \operatorname{TrivSqZeroExt}(k, V)$ to $A_k$ lying over the tangent base morphism, and a morphism $w_1$ from that spectrum to $U_e$, such that $w_0$ followed by $a_k$ witnesses `IsTangentOfPair` for the given pair (a Schlessinger map out of the pair ring $I$-construction together with a morphism from its spectrum restricting to the two members of the pair), $w_1$ followed by the open immersion equals the $L_k$-translate of $w_0$, and the map in question is the tangent-coordinate function of the associated chart ring homomorphism. The conclusion is the equality of functions $b_0 + c_s' = c_s + b_1$.
--
--   This is the coordinate form of the statement that the torsor of infinitesimal liftings is additive around a commuting square of automorphisms congruent to the identity modulo $I$: the two ways of passing from $u$ to the common composite $v_{T'} \circ \operatorname{Spec}\psi_0 = v_{A_1} \circ \operatorname{Spec}\psi_1$ give the same tangent coordinates. It is used in the deformation-theoretic comparison of charts for the Jacobian with good reduction, where the resulting difference of coordinate systems is realised as a derivation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_SmallExtension_isTangentCoordsOfPairAt_add_eq_add_of_specMap_comp_eq.lean

